title: Bodies that rotate
intro: Tick a body's Rotates and it turns: it tips over, spins, and gets knocked about, while everything else stays upright as before.
project: Empty | Tumble

# A floor 24 wide whose top is at y = -2.5, a platformer player, a crate dropped tilted, a tall plank stood on end, and
# a frozen plank tilted down to the floor as a ramp, its low end at the player's left.
create: Sprite
rename: Floor
set: Transform.Position = 0, -3, 0
set: Sprite.Size = 24, 1
set: Sprite.Tint = #4A4E5A
add: BoxCollider
set: BoxCollider.Size = 24, 1
deselect
create: Platformer Player
set: Transform.Position = -4, -2, 0
deselect
create: Crate
set: Transform.Position = -2, 1, 0
set: Transform.Rotation.Z = 30
deselect
create: Crate
rename: Plank
set: Transform.Position = 3, -1, 0
set: Sprite.Size = 0.3, 3
set: BoxCollider.Size = 0.3, 3
set: Body.Rotates = true
deselect
create: Crate
rename: Ramp
set: Transform.Position = -7, -1.95, 0
set: Transform.Rotation.Z = -15
set: Sprite.Size = 5, 0.3
set: Sprite.Tint = #7A7A80
set: BoxCollider.Size = 5, 0.3
set: Body.Rotates = true
set: Body.Frozen = true
expectcomponents: Crate = Transform, Sprite, BoxCollider, Body, Pushable

chapter: Tipping over | Body > Rotates
select: Crate
look: 0, -0.5, 4
explain: entity:Crate | A tilted crate | Here's a crate, turned thirty degrees and up in the air. Until now a body stayed upright whatever its rotation: it fell and landed as a flat, upright box.
set: Body.Rotates = true
explain: field:Body.Rotates | Rotates | Now a body has Rotates. Tick it, and its box collider turns with it, which the Scene view outlines.
play
wait: 2
expectat: Crate = -1.91, -2
expectvalue: Crate.Transform.Rotation.Z = 0 ~ 1
explain: game | Lands on its corner | It lands on its corner and tips over, then comes to rest flat, as a real crate would.
stop

chapter: Knocked about | Everything meets it turned
say: The tall plank on the right rotates too. The player doesn't: bodies without Rotates stay upright, as players and enemies should.
play
wait: 1
hold: Right 3
expectvalue: Plank.Transform.Rotation.Z = -90 ~ 3
explain: game | Shoved and tipped | Walking into the crate shoves it along by their weights, and the crate, hitting the plank low down, tips it over.
stop
select: Plank
explain: field:Body.Grip | Grip | Grip says how well it holds on to what it touches. Low, it slides off an edge like ice. High, it tips over instead.

chapter: Spinning, and ramps | Spin, and frozen turned planks
select: Crate
set: Body.Spin = 400
explain: field:Body.Spin | Spin | Spin is how fast it turns, in degrees a second. Set it, and the crate starts out spinning.
play
wait: 2
expectat: Crate = -1.47, -2
explain: game | Spun as it fell | It spun as it fell, tumbled on landing and settled again.
explain: entity:Ramp | A tilted ramp | The grey plank on the left rotates too, but it's frozen: a turned box that stays put, a ramp.
hold: Left 0.6
expectvalue: Player.Transform.Position.Y = -1.1 ~ 0.5
explain: game | Walked up | The player walks up its slant, as everything meets a turned box as it is: rays, shadows and the walls of tile, hex and isometric maps too.
stop
